# ParserTrace conventions

### Category hierarchy

Group prefixes enable entire groups. Leaves enable one stream. Full list
lives in `docs/08_TRACING.md`; `meridian trace categories` prints it live.

| Enum case | Raw value (CLI / env var string) |
|---|---|
| `.tokenize` | `tokenize` |
| `.parse` | `parse` |
| `.phraseParse` | `phrase.parse` |
| `.phraseMatch` | `phrase.match` |
| `.phraseExtractArgs` | `phrase.args` |
| `.phraseInline` | `phrase.inline` |
| `.statement` | `statement` |
| `.expression` | `expression` |
| `.lowering` | `lowering` |
| `.symbols` | `symbols` |
| `.merconfig` | `merconfig` |
| `.rulebook` | `rulebook` |
| `.skill` | `skill` |
| `.codegen` | `codegen` |
| `.diagnostics` | `diagnostics` |
| `.timing` | `timing` (off by default; excluded from `capturing()`'s default set) |

`.diagnostics` mirrors every `DiagnosticEngine`-reported `Diagnostic` into the
trace stream. `.timing` accumulates `trace.phase(_:)` spans (bootstrap
sub-phases, `symbols`/`parse`/`lower`/`codegen`) and prints an end-of-compile
profile; it's opt-in only, so `ParserTrace.capturing()` (no explicit
`categories:`) never includes it — pass `categories: [.timing]` explicitly to
assert timing output.

### `MERIDIAN_TRACE` env var

`ParserTrace()` reads `MERIDIAN_TRACE` **at init time** and auto-enables
categories. Both `ParserTrace.shared` and fresh `ParserTrace()` instances
read this env var. This means:
- Setting `MERIDIAN_TRACE=all swift test` activates tracing globally for that
  test run.
- Tests that create `ParserTrace()` will inherit env-var activation unless
  they call `disableAll()` explicitly.
- Use `ParserTrace.silent()` in tests that want guaranteed silence regardless
  of env var.

### Thread safety

`ParserTrace` is `@unchecked Sendable` with internal `NSLock` for all mutable
state. It is safe to call `log/push/pop` from concurrent contexts. In unit
tests, prefer a fresh `ParserTrace.capturing(…).trace` per test to avoid
cross-test output mixing.

### Adding a trace point

1. Optionally add a new `Category` case and its `rawValue` string.
2. Call `trace.log(.category, "…")` or `trace.push/pop` in the relevant method.
3. Add a `capturing(categories:)` test to `ParserTraceTests.swift`.

### The `trace` parameter convention

Every compiler component that can produce trace output takes
`trace: ParserTrace = .shared` as a constructor parameter.
- Default is `.shared` (works in production).
- Unit tests pass a fresh `ParserTrace()` (via `ParserTrace.capturing(categories:)`)
  or `ParserTrace.silent()`.
- The CLI never mutates `.shared`: `compile`, `check`, `verify`, `run`,
  `migrate-skill`, and `preview-skill` each build a fresh, isolated instance
  via `makeCLITrace(spec:file:)` (`Sources/MeridianCLIKit/CLISupport.swift`)
  from their own `--trace`/`--trace-file` options and thread it down into
  `Compiler`, `SkillMigrator`, `SkillMarkdownImporter`, and `ManifestEmitter`.

### No silent-trace components

Nothing in the compile pipeline is allowed to hardcode `.silent()` for a
`trace` it was handed — that would silently discard a caller's `--trace`
request. `SkillMigrator` and `SkillMarkdownImporter` both default their `trace`
parameter to `.shared`/the owning `Compiler`'s trace, never to `.silent()`;
only test call sites should pass `.silent()` explicitly.
